tus per paper is kept in authored/evidence-status.json.","citation_ids":["cite.long.thm-geometry"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.thm-geometry"],"id":"long.thm-geometry","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 1.8 (Achievement-set geometry)","locator":"Long record Theorem 1.8, p. 22, label thm:geometry","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*$\\mathcal{A}$ is compact, closed, perfect, totally disconnected and nowhere dense, and $\\operatorname{volume}(\\mathcal{A}) = 1$. Thus its measure is positive although it contains no interval. Its convex hull is $[0,E]$, where $E=\\sum_{n\\ge1}w_n$. The positive-index digit coding onto $\\mathcal{A}$ is injective: each achievable real has *exactly one* support.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-geometry","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-geometry","id":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-geometry%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_achievement_geometry%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/edges/%5B%22long.thm-geometry%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_achievement_geometry%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR20.paper_achievement_geometry"},{"derived":true,"family":"provenance","from":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.thm-geometry","id":"field:24ceb5b9c1ed51ed7ddda475ba4ce434b450a4277929e96bb162646a077628ad","kind":"source_id","owner_ref":"sha256:f31aeb6174afd909393ada9bc329cd29dc9b1b6a0de8f72a49f18ab372947af5/nodes/long.